  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Event log",
      "items": [
        "Edges named topic are rows in event_log, the Postgres table used as a queue",
        "Ordered consumers keep a cursor; evaluations are claimed with FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED",
        "The Investigator is the second consumer of the verdicts topic; state never waits for it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Read-only agents",
      "items": [
        "Graphs read, runners write: no tool has a side effect, and the runners open approval items",
        "Tools take the tenant from a closure; allowlists give the Investigator 11 tools, the Policy Agent 4, the Copilot all 13",
        "Remediation is a dry run unless five gates hold, including an approved item with a matching payload hash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Approval kinds",
      "items": [
        "remediation, policy_draft, evidence_request, tier3_interrupt",
        "Tier 3 runs on the agent core and pauses as a tier3_interrupt item",
        "reevaluate() re-pulls the connector so the new verdict supersedes the failing row; only the e2e test calls it, and there is no CLI command for it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Where the code differs from spec.md",
      "items": [
        "ccp run enqueues every (test, subject) pair; the impact step runs from ccp evaluate run --impact, the worker, and re-evaluation",
        "The Policy Agent runs only from ccp policy gap or draft; spec Layer 9 also calls it a verdicts consumer",
        "The parallel investigations topic is declared but never produced or consumed"
      ]
    }
  ]
